   "definition_quote": "In the \\emph{stopping rule} problem, the input consists of a stream of i.i.d samples $\\{X_t\\}_{t\\geq 1}$ drawn from a distribution over an a-priori known support $[-R,R]$ and with unknown mean $\\mu$. Given $\\epsStop,\\deltaStop \\in (0,1)$, the goal of the stopping rule is to halt after seeing as few samples as possible while releasing a $(1\\pm\\epsStop)$-approximation of $\\mu$ at halting time."
  }
